# eth0 configuration for PYNQ-Z2 -- STATIC, no DHCP, no alias.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why DHCP was removed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The original file was:
#
#   auto eth0
#   iface eth0 inet dhcp            <-- no DHCP server on a direct PC link
#
#   auto eth0:1
#   iface eth0:1 inet static
#   address 192.168.2.99
#   netmask 255.255.255.0
#
# With no DHCP server reachable, dhclient could not renew. It kept two stale
# leases from an earlier Internet-Connection-Sharing session
# (192.168.137.61 and 192.168.137.125) and cycled between them. Every switch
# removed the address for ~10 seconds. Observed directly:
#
#   17:19:23 inet 192.168.137.125
#   17:19:29 (no address)
#   17:19:41 inet 192.168.137.61
#   17:19:52 inet 192.168.137.125
#   17:20:02 (no address)
#   17:20:14 inet 192.168.137.61
#
# That is what made the browser picture freeze for a few seconds, come back,
# then freeze again -- and it also broke Jupyter's WebSocket ("Replacing stale
# connection" / "Starting buffering") and any long-lived HTTP stream.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why the eth0:1 alias was removed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The alias (192.168.2.99) made ifup fail at boot:
#
#   ifup[714]: cat: '/sys/class/net/eth0:1/ifindex': No such file or directory
#   ifup[729]: RTNETLINK answers: File exists
#   ifup[217]: ifup: failed to bring up eth0:1
#   systemd[1]: networking.service: Failed with result 'exit-code'.
#
# Because networking.service aborted, the static address was never applied and
# dhclient took over -- defeating the whole point. The alias is not needed for
# this project (the board is reached at 192.168.137.125), so it is dropped.
# If you ever want the documented 192.168.2.99 fallback back, add it as a
# second address on eth0 rather than as an eth0:1 alias.

auto eth0
iface eth0 inet static
    address 192.168.137.125
    netmask 255.255.255.0
    broadcast 192.168.137.255
